  "$comment": "Campaign level 18 (stretch 3): highland valleys full of wolf dens that hunt only the player (beastPrey player) while two rivals grow beyond a gorge. Clear the north valley; raze the sneaky tribe signal pyre that watches the northern pass; clear the south valley; pray at the gorge shrine to raise a land bridge east and an instant causeway to the wolf isle, a small island in the gorge that nothing can reach before the shrine (so its two packs cannot be cleared early); clear both isle packs (their dormant seer stone draws the bot there); pray away the turtle tribe ley stones (dormant until the isle is clear, six more posted guards arrive then, four fresh wardens march to pray the valley ley away, and from minute 14 the turtle tribe sends two fresh wardens a minute to pray each of its stones back while it stands) and keep two ley stones for two and a half minutes; then an instant causeway reaches the south gorge isle, where the two oldest packs den by a dormant seer: clear them and pray at it (the dens guard the seer, so the bot clears them first). The isle causeways are instant on purpose: a rising causeway to an awake site stalls the sim (see engine notes). Bot win about 25850.",
